# The BIG-IP admin group. Its members are the PRIVILEGED accounts — the ones the BIG-IP
# binds and evaluates — not the human identity entries under ou=people. Putting identities
# here would look right and grant nothing.
#
# Seeded after ldap/warden-users.ldif so the member DN already exists. Warden also stamps
# these accounts with the role attribute, because the BIG-IP cannot read OpenLDAP's memberOf
# (it is operational there): the group is the source of truth, the stamp is how the BIG-IP
# is told. In a directory that returns memberOf normally, such as AD, the group is read
# directly and no stamp is involved.
dn: ${WARDEN_ADMIN_GROUP_DN}
objectClass: groupOfNames
cn: ${WARDEN_ADMIN_GROUP_CN}
description: BIG-IP administrators — members are granted the administrator role
member: uid=alice.admin,${WARDEN_PRIV_SEARCH_BASE}
